# config/policy.vista.env - the Vista multimodal policy zoo (vision + finger camera + contact mic).
#
# Rickmer's fork: a separate vista/ package with its own Hydra entry (train_vista.py, config_path
# vista/config) and its own suite runner, so it needs a different entrypoint rather than a
# different config of docker/train.sh. Select with POLICY=vista. See
# docs/training-instructions.md § "Choosing a policy" and the fork's docs/VISTA_AGENT_GUIDE.md.
#
# train_day0suite.sh trains all eight suite models back to back unless you narrow it:
#   POLICY=vista DATASET=... ./train_policy.sh --model vista_vt

POLICY_DIR=external/polyumi_vista_policy
IMAGE=polyumi-vista
# No CONFIG_NAME: scripts/train_day0suite.sh passes --config-name=train_day0suite_workspace itself,
# once per suite model, so there is nothing here for the env var to steer.
TRAIN_CMD="bash docker/train_day0suite.sh"
# No SERVE_CMD: the fork's docker/serve.sh runs serve_policy.py, which is still the visuomotor
# UmiPolicyBackend -- it reads camera0_rgb and agent_pos only, and a Vista checkpoint also needs
# finger_rgb and mic_0. Serving Vista needs a backend that puts those on the wire; until then
# serve_policy.sh refuses POLICY=vista rather than failing inside the container.
